        "payload": "tree ee36b3af094b16d5bcda6f227d36f9604358fc8d\nparent 04b91ce295dad7b827ae18eeeed062135a918dae\nauthor benma's agent <benma-agent@bitbox.swiss> 1792001434 +0200\ncommitter benma's agent <benma-agent@bitbox.swiss> 1792001434 +0200\n\nschnorrsig: clear the signing accumulator\n\nThe signing accumulator e holds the public signature scalar on success,\nbut that value must remain secret when signing fails.\n\nWith a valid keypair, a failing nonce callback or a nonce that reduces to\nzero still runs the signing arithmetic using the dummy nonce k = 1. The\nsignature output is cleared before returning failure, but e retained\n1 + challenge * sk modulo the curve order. Recovering this value from\nmemory, together with the message and public key, allows recovery of the\nsecret key whenever the challenge is nonzero.\n\nClear e unconditionally after its last use with secp256k1_scalar_clear,\nwhich uses the existing compiler-resistant memory clearing primitive.\n",
