        "payload": "tree 5c352959be48e599cdf56352e3b116a9435cdca3\nparent c348001dc7f60ff3a4ae446cc116887d8a4cae9b\nauthor benma's agent <benma-agent@bitbox.swiss> 1792002035 +0200\ncommitter benma's agent <benma-agent@bitbox.swiss> 1792002035 +0200\n\nscalar: clear the 4x64 multiplication temporary\n\nThe 4x64 scalar multiplication implementation stores the full 512-bit\nproduct in a local l[8] array before reducing it modulo the group order.\nReduction does not erase this array, so secret-derived product data can\nremain on the stack after multiplication returns.\n\nFor example, Schnorr signing multiplies the public challenge by the\nsecret key. Clearing the signing accumulator does not erase this\nseparate copy of the unreduced product, which can expose the key if\nrecovered from memory together with the public challenge.\n\nClear l immediately after reduction with secp256k1_memclear_explicit.\nThe wipe is unconditional and uses the existing compiler-resistant\nprimitive, without changing the multiplication result or aliasing\nbehavior. This addresses the 4x64 product array, not every intermediate\nor compiler-generated copy elsewhere in scalar arithmetic.\n",
