      "updated_at": "2026-10-15T08:47:08Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "On arm64 the clear costs nothing above noise: `scalar_mul` takes 22.2 ns on master and on this PR with 4x64, 56.9 ns versus 57.1 ns on 8x32 with `l[16]` also cleared, and verify and sign do not move. The clear is not dropped and calls no memset: `scalar_mul_512` is an out-of-line call that writes the product to `l` on the stack, and the library's `scalar_mul` zeroes it with two 32-byte stores. Method: median of the best time over 7 interleaved Release runs per variant, 8x32 forced with `SECP256K1_TEST_OVERRIDE_WIDE_MULTIPLY=int64`; x86_64 and its assembly path not measured.\n",
